This code creates a sorting algorithms visualizer with the specified requirements. The `SortingVisualizer` class has methods for initializing the canvas, drawing the array elements, drawing the controls, and implementing the various sorting algorithms.

The `home()` method initializes the canvas and draws the initial state of the array. The `scramble()` method generates a random array to sort. The `setSpeed()` method sets the animation speed, and the `toggleStep()` method toggles between step-by-step and continuous animation.

The `draw()` method renders the current state of the array on the canvas. The `drawControls()` method creates and renders the control elements on the HTML page. The `drawStack()` method renders the call stack for recursive algorithms.

The `algorithm()` method determines which sorting algorithm to run based on the selected option in the dropdown menu. The `bubble()`, `quick()`, `merge()`, `heap()`, and `radix()` methods implement the corresponding sorting algorithms.

The `swap()` method swaps two elements in the array and updates the comparison and swap counters. The `sleep()` method pauses the execution for a specified period of time to control the animation speed.

